From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jim Martin <jimmartin@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 17:51:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] drm/msm/dp: read the link capabilities afresh for every sink

msm_dp_panel_read_dpcd() fills panel->link_info but never clears it.
Since commit ed100aa239be ("drm/msm/dp: Enable support for eDP v1.4+
link rates table") the MAX_LINK_RATE path only runs while
link_info->rate is still 0, so after the first external sink every
later one keeps the first one's link rate until reboot. A monitor that
follows a slower one is trained below its maximum, and modes that need
the extra bandwidth are rejected; one that follows a faster monitor is
first trained above its maximum. use_rate_set, rate_set and the rate
table are kept in the same way.

Clear link_info before reading the sink's capabilities.

Fixes: ed100aa239be ("drm/msm/dp: Enable support for eDP v1.4+ link rates table")
Assisted-by: Opus 5.5
Signed-off-by: Jim Martin <jimmartin@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dp/dp_panel.c | 6 +++++-
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dp/dp_panel.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dp/dp_panel.c
index e76dad0f666..909695902e5 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dp/dp_panel.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dp/dp_panel.c
@@ -95,12 +95,16 @@ static int msm_dp_panel_read_dpcd(struct msm_dp_panel *msm_dp_panel)
 
 	panel = container_of(msm_dp_panel, struct msm_dp_panel_private, msm_dp_panel);
 	dpcd = msm_dp_panel->dpcd;
+	link_info = &msm_dp_panel->link_info;
+
+	/* Nothing read from an earlier sink may carry over to this one */
+	memset(link_info, 0, sizeof(*link_info));
+
 	rc = drm_dp_read_dpcd_caps(panel->aux, dpcd);
 	if (rc)
 		return rc;
 
 	msm_dp_panel->vsc_sdp_supported = drm_dp_vsc_sdp_supported(panel->aux, dpcd);
-	link_info = &msm_dp_panel->link_info;
 	link_info->revision = dpcd[DP_DPCD_REV];
 	major = (link_info->revision >> 4) & 0x0f;
 	minor = link_info->revision & 0x0f;
-- 
